  "notes": "Governmental funds on a modified cash basis (Total Governmental Funds 2022 column printed on p6, labels on p5; balance sheet totals on p4); proprietary funds on the accrual basis (measure net position; the proprietary cash flow statement p9 is not recorded in 'proprietary', as in FY2023-FY2025). Fund balances recorded as fund balance (313,422 -> 338,363); cash = cash in bank + cash with county treasurer, certificates of deposit as investments (p4, 2022 and 2021 columns); the cash change differs from the fund balance change by the 83 increase in certificates of deposit. Statement lines split with the report's own fund schedules: Taxes 33,048 = General property 3,365 + motor vehicle 2,972 (p10) + Street property 16,900 + county road tax 1,292 (p14) + nonmajor property 8,519 (p12); Intergovernmental revenues 111,104 = General 46,911 (p10) + Street 64,193 (p14); Charges for services 45,746 = Schedule 2 licenses 4,031 + materials and services sold 40,152 + sales tax collected 1,563. Capital outlay 33,033 (General 14,533 + Street 18,500) has no printed function on the statement row; only the Street Fund piece is labelled with its function. No transfers in FY2022. Balance sheet: government-wide Statement of Net Position (p1), since its governmental column includes capital assets 995,240. Detail: Schedule 2 (General Fund), Schedule 4 (Fire, Cemetery), Schedule 6 (Street, Keno Lottery), Schedule 8 (proprietary funds combined, Actual column; zero non-operating capital purchase lines skipped). Not recorded to avoid double counting: Schedule 7 budget comparison (fund totals only) and Schedule 9 Keno budget-basis reconciliation; Schedules 3 and 5 are balance sheets. Read pages 1-17 of 17"
}
